  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be the function given by $f(x)= e^(- x^(2))$.\n\n(a) Write the first four nonzero terms and the general term of the Taylor series for $f$ about $x = 0$.\n\n(b) Use your answer to part (a) to find $lim_(x -> 0) frac(1 - x^(2)- f(x),x^(4))$.\n\n(c) Write the first four nonzero terms of the Taylor series for $integral_(0)^(x) e^(- t^(2)) d t$ about $x = 0$. Use the first two terms of your answer to estimate $integral_(0)^(1 \\/ 2) e^(- t^(2)) d t$.\n\n(d) Explain why the estimate found in part (c) differs from the actual value of $integral_(0)^(1 \\/ 2) e^(- t^(2)) d t$ by less than $frac(1,200)$.",
